                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239526876",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198076616061",
                            "num_reviews": 95,
                            "playtime_forever": 117,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 11,
                            "playtime_at_review": 117,
                            "last_played": 1793990365
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] NO! [/h1]\n\nOut of pure, twisted curiosity, I ended up spending about two hours in this game. The first hour was nothing but a painful realization that absolutely nothing works the way the developer intended. The game is utterly broken. The trailer on store preview on Steam is a total scam, and it makes you question how Steam's quality control could greenlight this—let alone allow a broken Early Access title to sell paid DLCs.\nLet’s look at the facts: this game has been stuck in Early Access since 2016. That is also the exact same year it received its very last update. Not that any updates would have saved it, but this corpse has simply been floating dead in the Steam store ever since.\nAt its core, the game tries to copy The Binding of Isaac. Key word: tries. Since it doesn't actually work, it raises a profound philosophical question: is it even a game anymore, or just a digital monument to human error?\nThe absolute peak of my experience came when I accidentally clicked on something in the main menu. Steam instantly rewarded me with an achievement. This permanent badge of my own stupidity will now haunt my profile showcase until the end of time.\nVerdict: Do not make the same mistake I did. Value your time. Do not buy it, do not download it, do not launch it. Do not give this title a single second more of your attention than it took to read this warning. No Turning Back is an accurate title—because once you buy it, there is no turning back from the regret.",
